description: Patterns for AI job processing using Supabase Edge Functions, centralized job API clients, and real-time progress tracking for training and inference operations.
globs: 
alwaysApply: false
---
- **Use Supabase Edge Functions for Job Processing**
  - All training and inference jobs must use edge functions to avoid overloading Next.js server
  - Reference [training-start](mdc:supabase/functions/training-start/index.ts) and [inference-start](mdc:supabase/functions/inference-start/index.ts) for implementation patterns
  - Use service role key for database operations in edge functions
  - Always validate user ownership before processing jobs

- **Job API Client Usage**
  - Use the centralized [jobs API client](mdc:frontend/src/lib/api/jobs.ts) for all job operations
  - Import types from [jobs.ts](mdc:frontend/src/types/jobs.ts) for type safety
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Use the jobs API client
  import { useJobsApi } from '@/lib/api/jobs';
  import type { TrainingStartRequest, InferenceStartRequest } from '@/types/jobs';
  
  const jobsApi = useJobsApi();
  const result = await jobsApi.startTraining({
    user_id: userId,
    face_model_id: faceModelId,
    image_metadata: { urls: imageUrls, total_images: imageUrls.length }
  });
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Make direct fetch calls to edge functions
  const response = await fetch('/functions/v1/training-start', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: JSON.stringify(data)
  });
  ```

- **Real-time Progress Tracking**
  - Always use [progress hooks](mdc:frontend/src/hooks/useJobProgress.ts) for real-time updates
  - Enable Supabase realtime subscriptions by default with polling fallback
  - Handle completion and error states properly
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Use specialized progress hooks
  import { useTrainingProgress, useInferenceProgress } from '@/hooks/useJobProgress';
  
  const { data, progress, isComplete, error } = useTrainingProgress(jobId, userId, {
    onComplete: (data) => {
      toast.success('Training completed!');
      router.push('/models');
    },
    onError: (error) => {
      toast.error(`Training failed: ${error.message}`);
    }
  });
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Use manual polling or useState for progress
  const [progress, setProgress] = useState(0);
  useEffect(() => {
    const interval = setInterval(async () => {
      const response = await fetch(`/api/progress/${jobId}`);
      const data = await response.json();
      setProgress(data.progress);
    }, 1000);
    return () => clearInterval(interval);
  }, [jobId]);
  ```

- **Job Status Management**
  - Follow the defined status flows: pending → processing → completed/failed
  - For inference jobs, handle queued status when face models aren't ready
  - Use the `is_complete` flag to determine when to stop tracking
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Handle all job statuses
  const renderJobStatus = (status: string, progress: number) => {
    switch (status) {
      case 'queued':
        return <Badge variant="secondary">Queued - waiting for face model</Badge>;
      case 'pending':
        return <Badge variant="default">Starting...</Badge>;
      case 'processing':
        return <Progress value={progress} className="w-full" />;
      case 'completed':
        return <Badge variant="success">Completed</Badge>;
      case 'failed':
        return <Badge variant="destructive">Failed</Badge>;
      default:
        return <Badge variant="outline">Unknown</Badge>;
    }
  };
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Only handle basic status without considering queue states
  const status = job.status === 'completed' ? 'Done' : 'Processing';
  ```

- **Error Handling and User Feedback**
  - Always provide user feedback for job operations using toast notifications
  - Handle network errors, authentication failures, and job-specific errors
  - Show loading states during job creation and progress tracking
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Comprehensive error handling with user feedback
  const handleStartTraining = async () => {
    setIsLoading(true);
    try {
      const result = await jobsApi.startTraining(requestData);
      toast.success(`Training started! Estimated time: ${result.estimated_duration}s`);
      setCurrentJobId(result.job_id);
    } catch (error) {
      const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Failed to start training';
      toast.error(message);
      console.error('Training start error:', error);
    } finally {
      setIsLoading(false);
    }
  };
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Silent failures or generic error handling
  try {
    await jobsApi.startTraining(data);
  } catch (error) {
    console.log('Error occurred');
  }
  ```

- **Job Queue Management**
  - Use [useJobQueue](mdc:frontend/src/hooks/useJobProgress.ts) hook for managing multiple jobs
  - Show queue position for inference jobs when face models aren't ready
  - Provide clear information about job dependencies
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Use job queue hook for comprehensive job management
  const { 
    jobs, 
    activeJobs, 
    queuedJobs, 
    processingJobs, 
    completedJobs 
  } = useJobQueue(userId, 'inference');
  
  return (
    <div>
      <Section title="Active Jobs" jobs={activeJobs} />
      <Section title="Queue" jobs={queuedJobs} />
      <Section title="Completed" jobs={completedJobs} />
    </div>
  );
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Track jobs manually with individual state
  const [trainingJobs, setTrainingJobs] = useState([]);
  const [inferenceJobs, setInferenceJobs] = useState([]);
  ```

- **Database Integration**
  - Reference [job tables migration](mdc:supabase/migrations/20241227_create_job_tables.sql) for schema
  - Use proper UUID types for job IDs and foreign keys
  - Leverage RLS policies - users can only access their own jobs
  - Use JSONB for flexible settings storage in inference jobs

- **Progress UI Components**
  - Show elapsed time and estimated remaining time
  - Display meaningful progress messages (preprocessing, training epochs, etc.)
  - Use progress bars for visual feedback
  - Handle indeterminate progress for queued jobs
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Rich progress display with time estimates
  const ProgressDisplay = ({ data }: { data: TrainingProgressResponse }) => (
    <div className="space-y-2">
      <div className="flex justify-between text-sm">
        <span>{data.status}: {data.progress}%</span>
        <span>
          {data.elapsed_time}s elapsed, ~{data.estimated_remaining}s remaining
        </span>
      </div>
      <Progress value={data.progress} />
      <p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground">
        Processing {data.image_count} images for face model training
      </p>
    </div>
  );
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Basic progress bar without context
  <Progress value={progress} />
  ```

- **Authentication and Security**
  - Always pass user_id in job requests for validation
  - Use Supabase session tokens for edge function authentication
  - Validate face model ownership before starting jobs
  - Never expose service role keys in frontend code

- **Performance Considerations**
  - Use realtime subscriptions instead of frequent polling when possible
  - Implement proper cleanup for subscriptions and polling intervals
  - Set reasonable timeouts for long-running operations (5 minutes default)
  - Use debouncing for UI updates to prevent excessive re-renders

- **Mock vs Production**
  - Current implementation uses mock Modal API calls for testing
  - All timing and progress steps are simulated
  - When migrating to real Modal API, update edge functions only
  - Frontend code should work unchanged with real API

- **Documentation References**
  - See [Job API Documentation](mdc:docs/JOB_APIS.md) for complete implementation guide
  - Reference edge function implementations for API patterns
  - Follow TypeScript interfaces for request/response structures
